00:04:00,000 --> 00:04:06,000
A comedy about growing up… and the bumps along the way.

2
00:08:00,000 --> 00:08:06,000
Juno is a comedy, drama, romance film directed by Jason Reitman.

3
00:12:00,000 --> 00:12:06,000
Faced with an unplanned pregnancy, sixteen year old high-schooler, Juno
MacGuff, makes an unusual decision regarding her unborn child.

4
00:16:00,000 --> 00:16:06,000
Juno MacGuff, played by Elliot Page.

5
00:20:00,000 --> 00:20:06,000
Paulie Bleeker, played by Michael Cera.

6
00:24:00,000 --> 00:24:06,000
Vanessa Loring, played by Jennifer Garner.

7
00:28:00,000 --> 00:28:06,000
Mark Loring, played by Jason Bateman.

8
00:32:00,000 --> 00:32:06,000
Mac MacGuff, played by J.K. Simmons.

9
00:36:00,000 --> 00:36:06,000
Bren MacGuff, played by Allison Janney.

10
00:40:00,000 --> 00:40:06,000
Juno is a 2007 American coming-of-age comedy-drama film
directed by Jason Reitman and written by Diablo Cody.

11
00:44:00,000 --> 00:44:06,000
Elliot Page stars as the title character, an independent-minded teenager confronting her
unplanned pregnancy and the subsequent events that put pressures of adult life onto her.

12
00:48:00,000 --> 00:48:06,000
Michael Cera, Jennifer Garner, Jason Bateman, Allison Janney and J.

13
00:52:00,000 --> 00:52:06,000
Simmons also star.

14
00:56:00,000 --> 00:56:06,000
Filming took place in 2007 in Vancouver, British Columbia.

15
01:00:00,000 --> 01:00:06,000
It premiered on September 8 at the 2007 Toronto International
Film Festival, receiving a standing ovation.

16
01:04:00,000 --> 01:04:06,000
Juno won the Academy Award for Best Original Screenplay and earned three other nominations for Best Picture, Best Director for Reitman, and
Best Actress for 20-year old Page (who was presenting as female at the time, and is the sixth-youngest nominee in the category).

17
01:08:00,000 --> 01:08:06,000
The film's soundtrack, featuring several songs performed by Kimya Dawson in various guises, was the first
chart-topping soundtrack since 2006's Dreamgirls and Fox Searchlight's first number-one soundtrack.

18
01:12:00,000 --> 01:12:06,000
Juno earned back its initial budget of $6.5 million in twenty days, the first
nineteen of which were when the film was in limited release.

19
01:16:00,000 --> 01:16:06,000
It went on to earn $232.3 million worldwide.

20
01:20:00,000 --> 01:20:06,000
Juno received acclaim from critics, many of whom placed the
film on their top-ten lists for the year.

21
01:24:00,000 --> 01:24:06,000
It has received criticism and praise from members of both the anti-abortion and
abortion rights communities regarding its treatment of abortion.

22
01:28:00,000 --> 01:28:06,000
The film explores themes of puberty, first time,
becoming an adult, sexuality, pregnancy.

23
01:32:00,000 --> 01:32:06,000
The tone is lighthearted and uplifting and emotional.
